<title>MEXICO: Aeromex and CMA shares end Mexico listing.</title>
<headline>Aeromex and CMA shares end Mexico listing.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares issued by airline Aerovias de Mexico (Aeromex) and Corporacion Mexicana de Aviacion (CMA) will no longer be listed on the Mexican Stock Exchange (BMV) after Wednesday due to a swap with shares listed by their controlling company, Cintra, the stock exchange said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Aeromexico and CMA, or Mexicana, told the stock exchange that they will still be bound to exchange 16.096438 A or CPO series share and 12.495919 A series shares, respectively, for one Cintra A series share.</p>
<p>--Karina Balderas, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9562</p>
